WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.103
Braces hurt.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.210
And it's no wonder.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:11.150
Your teeth aren't supposed
to move like that,

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.850
but there's more happening
here than meets the eye.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.710
Braces don't work the
way you probably think

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.820
because they don't just
shift your teeth around.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.512
They have to break down your jawbone first.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.820
Americans pay up to $7,500
for braces per person,

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.073
but it's worth it.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.780
And not just for that
perfect, Instagrammable smile.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.210
You see, misaligned teeth
are tricky to clean,

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.770
increasing your risk of tooth decay,

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:48.513
gum disease, or even tooth loss.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:53.330
That's where braces can help
straighten out the problem.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:56.006
But moving teeth is no easy feat

00:00:56.006 --> 00:00:58.130
because there's something in the way:

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.500
your jawbone.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.910
Now, the orthodontist
doesn't take out a drill

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.360
and break your jaw themselves.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.220
Instead, they trick your body into doing

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:07.463
the hard work for them.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:11.443
That's where braces come in.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.670
The wires are tightened across your teeth

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:18.030
in order to create
pressure against your gums.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.940
In turn, that pressure
constricts blood flow

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.720
to the tissue that holds
your teeth in place,

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.120
sort of like squeezing a
hose to stop the water.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.790
And without blood, the
tissue cells start to die.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.510
Now, normally, that
would be a major problem

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.760
because without that supportive tissue,

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.550
your teeth could fall out.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:39.370
But, in this case, that's exactly

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:42.093
what the doctor, or, dentist, ordered.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.900
Because your immune system
rushes to the rescue,

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:49.310
sending in special cells
called osteoclasts,

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.180
which ultimately relieve the pressure

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.000
and restore blood flow.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.890
They do this by sucking away
the calcium from your jaw bone.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:00.823
Yep, the cells are literally
dissolving your bone.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.840
It may sound like an extreme
solution to the problem,

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.520
but the result is a nice
hole in your jawbone

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.120
where the tooth can move in

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:12.590
away from the wires and all that pressure,

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.370
ultimately restoring blood flow

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.320
so that the tissue stays alive

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.343
and your teeth don't fall out.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.573
But you don't just do all of this once.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.800
People with braces have to check in

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.500
with their orthodontist regularly

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.620
because they need their braces retightened

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.963
so more teeth can move into place.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.570
And the more teeth you have to move,

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.703
the longer the braces will be on.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.440
Typically it takes
months to a couple years

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.498
to get the job done, but, eventually,

00:02:47.498 --> 00:02:48.770
the ordeal ends,

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.750
the braces come off for good,

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.841
and you can enjoy your new smile.

